From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0432-gfx-03-temp-buffer-release.patch

Source: 0432-gfx-03-temp-buffer-release.patch
buffers

Core patch on core-t33 (T35 stack), off unless EDEN_NX2_TC_TEMP_BUFFER_FRAMES is set.

Image copies between formats go through a device-local copy buffer from
TextureCacheRuntime::GetTemporaryBuffer: one buffer per power of two, made at the size of the
largest copy of that class and kept for the session. A 2560x1440 RGBA copy takes the 16 MiB one, a
4096x4096 32-bit copy the 64 MiB one; the set stays after the targets that needed them are gone.
EDEN_NX2_TC_TEMP_BUFFER_FRAMES=600 destroys a copy buffer no copy used for 600 frames once the GPU
is past the last copy recorded with it (the scheduler's IsFree, as the decode images use); the next
copy of that size makes it again.

Logs once "EDEN_NX2_TC_TEMP_BUFFER_FRAMES=600: copy buffers unused for 600 frames are destroyed"
and "Copy buffer of N MiB unused for F frames: destroyed" for each one; the sum of those sizes is
the saving, which run 149's logs do not show (a guess: tens of MiB, at most about 128).

Unset, kept for the session as before. Not built, not run.

